            "stem": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The inner membrane of the mitochondrion has a much larger surface area than the outer membrane because of the presence of cristae.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 19
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Different cell types vary in the number of cristae present per mitochondrion. Cardiac muscle cells have mitochondria with a very large number of cristae.",
                "source": {
                  "qp": 19
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Suggest  <b>and</b> explain why cardiac muscle cells have mitochondria with very large numbers of cristae.",
